      "short_description": "Historic outdoor stadium in Pasadena hosting a storied annual college-football championship game and a popular monthly flea market.",
      "number_of_stations": null,
      "cuisine_description": null,
      "overall_description": "The Rose Bowl Stadium is an iconic, historic outdoor venue located in Pasadena, California, famously recognized as a National Historic Landmark. It serves as a primary hub for major sporting events, including the annual Rose Bowl Game, as well as high-profile concerts and the monthly Rose Bowl Flea Market. While the facility reflects its age, it remains a beloved bucket-list destination for millions due to its rich tradition, scenic mountain surroundings, and unparalleled atmosphere. Visitors are encouraged to plan ahead for transport and parking, as the massive venue creates significant activity during major events.",
      "service_description": null,
      "ambience_description": "The stadium exudes a grand, nostalgic atmosphere, defined by its rich history and the high-energy vibe of the massive crowds that gather here for world-class events.",
      "amenities_description": "The venue is equipped with a variety of concession stands, ample restroom facilities, and merchandise areas, complemented by organized stadium tours that provide behind-the-scenes access.",
      "unique_selling_points": "As a National Historic Landmark, it is world-renowned for hosting the annual Rose Bowl Game and serving as a premier site for global concerts and historic sporting events.",
      "neighborhood_description": "The surrounding neighborhood offers a blend of historic charm and natural beauty, characterized by its proximity to the Arroyo Seco parkland and the vibrant shops and dining of Old Town Pasadena.",
      "physical_setting_description": "Situated in a scenic valley in Pasadena, this historic outdoor stadium is surrounded by lush landscaping and mountains. It serves as a prominent landmark that blends into the natural beauty of its Arroyo Seco setting.",
